WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.158
The bag is light. Why does it feel heavy?

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:06.316
Several demands can sit inside one load.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:09.474
Stress guidance considers responses and resources.

00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:12.632
Tests, conflict and change can create demands.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:15.789
The same event can feel different in context.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:22.105
Demands may exceed available resources.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:28.421
Heart rate, muscles and attention may change.

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:34.737
Break a global burden into concrete tasks.

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:41.053
What can change? Who could help?

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:44.211
Changing thoughts cannot solve every stressor.

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.368
Rest, conditions and practical help also matter.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:50.526
Physical symptoms need appropriate attention.

00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:56.842
Sort what to delay, share or seek help for.

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:03.158
Turn overwhelm into a concrete request.

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:06.316
Find reliable support for persistent distress.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:09.474
Feeling burdened does not mean lacking effort.

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:12.632
Rest and help-seeking can be actions.

00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.789
A shoulder need not carry everything alone.
